+## [2.0.1] — Unreleased
+
+### Fixed
+
+* `Calendrical.Persian` looks up its new years for Gregorian 1900 to 2100 in a table, `priv/astronomy/persian_new_years.csv`, where it worked out the equinox and true noon on every call, about 100 µs on Astro 2.8's ephemeris; `mix calendrical.astronomy_tables` writes the table from the astronomy and checks it with `--check`.
+
 ## [2.0.0] — 2026-10-24
 
 Calendrical 2.0 rebuilds every calendar on a kernel of eight callbacks and derives the rest. The [migration guide](https://hexdocs.pm/calendrical/migration.html) describes each change in full.
